+Pushed implementation commits
+=============================
+V8 recheck: a8cc9037638ca1bfb0c074f310df9973aa6b875e on codex/regex-v8-divergences.
+Native base: origin/main 50045bd. Branch: codex/regex-native-fixes.
+1. 1c8cb692e4ead491983b3bf828dd466419a20f23: class octal and quantifier order.
+2. 5bce1185a0c1b794c2f40bc95d964898ad426035: duplicate class-string endpoints.
+3. c63a961be1f617f0ed9b3bffc0a0b2cfaa051821: cached UTF-16 input view.
+4. d4dfab69b7442c32bf58cfcfb116c276302ad9d7: compound-write refusal.
+5. e806c6672a829ec07a9e5bd46e2ce54f393dfab1: long backtracking leak oracle.
+Each implementation step was pushed separately. No PR was opened.
+
+Five-line summary
+=================
+Annex B class octal now matches Node; the cohere near-2^63 pattern is accepted.
+Duplicate class strings no longer create exponential duplicate choice points.
+The input string owns a reusable UTF-16 view, invalidated on append and freed with it.
+Compound group/property writes stop with NotYet before native field lookup.
+The exact long fixture agrees with Node; removing its heap-frame free leaks 82,773 allocations.
+
+Pinned Node/V8 recheck
+=====================
+node --version: v24.19.0. V8: 13.6.233.17-node.51. Linux x64.
+The exact integration program prints, one line each:
+2
