+Spec answers: 4 / 2 / true / false / true / a|.
+The Linux output is identical to integration's supplied official darwin-arm64
+24.19.0 output and its earlier macOS 24.14.1 output. Mac results were supplied,
+not locally measured. No observed platform/version difference in these lines.
+
+Draft                            Reproduces on 24.19.0       Decision
+1. Singleton class folding        Yes, integration line 3     Refusal kept
+2. Scoped modifiers               Yes, integration lines 4/5  Refusals kept; missing legacy shape added
+3. Mixed empty class strings      Yes, line 6 and replace hang Refusal kept
+4. Unicode non-word boundary      Yes, integration line 1     Node-compatible runtime kept; no refusal
+5. Negative word lookahead        Yes, integration line 2     Node-compatible runtime kept; no refusal
+
+No existing refusal was dropped. All five reproducing drafts remain for Kirk;
+nothing was filed. The uppercase mixed-empty exec witness does not independently
+prove empty-first ordering: the folding defect can fail the nonempty alternative.
+The direct lowercase non-i ordering control agrees with the spec. Draft 3 also
+pins a separate replacement slow-path hang. The recheck's docs state this distinction.
+See docs/regexp-v8-divergences.md at a8cc903, and that branch's node2419 reports.
+Recheck totals: 13 explicit spec/Node witnesses; 4,650 generated visible cases;
+3,660 accepted executions, zero disagreements. Refusals cost zero patterns in the
+5,746-pattern parser corpus, zero test262 files there, and zero of 127,369 exec calls.
+Both metered/unlimited C configurations retained 127,369 test262 and 9,911 random
+comparisons with zero disagreements; 89 random inputs were loudly refused on that
+policy branch (83 unique pattern/flag pairs). Native-fixes below uses the main base,
+not a merge of the separate V8 refusal-policy branch.
