+First requested fix on regex-remaining, before the remaining-library claim.
+Merged main ef3d907 with matcher 50a1dc8, protocol ffb3ae0, V8 a8cc903,
+native fixes c962ce2, validity runner af12899. Merge commits preserve both
+regular search and V8 compatibility. Generated counts need full regeneration
+after the merged fresh analysis learns the protocol operations.
+
+Node v24.19.0, V8 13.6.233.17-node.51, Linux x64. Setup retry: ready steps
+0s each, build cache warm 180s, done 180s; nproc 5, CPU quota 4.
+Initial setup failed while sources were mid-merge. Old Go build-cache artifacts
+were removed after the 32 GiB filesystem filled; 6,443,376,895 bytes reclaimed.
+
+The a8cc903 exec fix does not fix split. Native disagreed on 5/8 supplied
+pattern/input pairs. Emitted JavaScript disagreed on two u pairs because lowering
+replaced an omitted split limit with 4294967295. Other requested entry points
+already agreed. The expanded fixture now covers exec, test, match, matchAll,
+replace, replaceAll, search, split, and omitted/undefined/numeric limit controls.
+
+Split candidate scans reproduce V8: default or Smi limit scans UTF-16 units;
+HeapNumber limit under u advances by Unicode code point, while v still scans
+units. Empty successful matches retain AdvanceStringIndex behavior. Numeric
+limits with an unproved V8 tag refuse for known sensitive u shapes, or unknown
+regex sources. Unaffected constant patterns and immutable regex lists remain
+accepted. A refused fixture pins double-array 100 versus literal 100: equal
+values produce different Node split results. Immediate numeric literals prove
+their tag; no runtime tag is guessed. Source and argument evaluation preserved.
+
+The forced regular engine missed 24/2659 V8 edge cases after merging. Unicode
+non-word-boundary assertions now use the VM fallback, which tries pair interiors.
+All 2659 pass in budgeted, forced-regular/fallback, and unlimited-VM modes.
+
+Node-only mutant: isolated C runtime copy replaced split's failed-candidate
+code-unit advance with AdvanceStringIndex. It compiled; Node and mutant both
+exited 0, with empty stderr and no sanitizer failures. Their stdout differed,
+so only the comparison with Node caught it. Outputs retained alongside report.
+
+Commands (all test output directed to logs):
+go test ./internal/oracle -run TestNativeAgreesWithNode/internal/oracle/testdata/regexp_surrogate -count=1 -v
+go test ./internal/native -run TestRegExpBytecodeV8Node -count=1 -v
+go test ./internal/oracle -run TestNativeAgreesWithNode/internal/oracle/testdata/sweeps/regexp_methods -count=1 -v
+go test ./internal/oracle -run TestRegExpSurrogateCounts -count=1 -v -args -update-regexp-surrogate-counts
+go test ./internal/lower -count=1
+
+All above passed. Full merged counts attempt is blocked by existing protocol
+operations missing from main's fresh.regexCall whitelist; those remain measured
+library work for the claim. Full uncached gate not yet run. The first baseline
+survey was discarded after concurrent header edits contaminated linking; the
+survey of record runs in a frozen checkout with the validity runner, stock tsc
+6.0.3, adaptation enabled, and a 60-second execution limit.
+
+Final core command:
+go test ./internal/regexp ./internal/native -run 'TestMatcher(Test262Executions|RandomNode)|TestRegExpBytecode(Test262|RandomNode|V8Node)' -count=1 -v
+Go: 127369 extracted executions plus 10000 random cases, all three modes,
+zero disagreements. Native: 127369 extracted executions plus 9911 accepted
+random cases, all three modes, zero disagreements; 89 random inputs retain
+the existing explicit V8 compatibility refusals. V8 edge cases 2659, all modes,
+zero disagreements. Regular-eligible extracted executions 127018 (six more
+now take the VM fallback). Go package 7.092s, native package 100.876s.
+
+Follow-up: numeric-limit safety examines compiled assertion instructions instead
+of pattern substrings. Nested negative assertions cannot evade the guard.
+New refused witness /(?!(?:\W))/u with a double-array limit is recorded.
+The surrogate fixtures and complete methods sweep pass after this change:
+go test ./internal/oracle -run 'TestNativeAgreesWithNode/internal/oracle/testdata/(regexp_surrogate|sweeps)' -count=1 -v
